## Q1-C resource audit — conditional logical map is now usable, but the application gate remains open

Draft PR #1449 provides the first content-bound production-resource map for the frozen R6M support objective. Its strongest defensible result is narrow and useful:

- under an explicit all-to-all compute/rotate/uncompute parity-ladder template, noncentral frame excess support maps to 4 logical two-qubit Clifford entanglers per coordinate and central excess support to 2;
- Tag and factored Restore terms map to declared controlled-Pauli logical operations under the same native-control convention;
- the fixed three-block family contains exactly nine arbitrary-angle rotations independent of frame support.

The PR correctly returns `PARTIAL_RESOURCE_MAP`, not a hardware result. It does **not** bind routing, cancellation, logical depth, rotation precision/synthesis, T count/depth, code distance, factories, physical qubits, spacetime or failure probability. Its internal QG-21 cross-check is adverse at the primary setting: donor-exact on 90/90 chemistry rows; only the registered sensitivity improves 18/90, by two logical two-qubit Cliffords. Preserve that null/adverse evidence.

Current prior art makes a broad compiler-resource headline especially unsafe. Symphony (arXiv:2608.11579, submitted 2026-08-12; current v2 visible in August 2026) performs global binary-symplectic controlled-Pauli Clifford simplification and reports on HamLib average reductions of 59% in two-qubit gates and 91% in circuit depth, with the public PHOENIX repository treating Symphony as the newer holistic compiler. Therefore Q1 cannot infer production advantage merely from a bounded auxiliary-support normal form.

### Next content-bound experiment

Freeze one architecture-level benchmark packet before inspecting outcomes:

1. public Hamiltonian instances and exact coefficients/angles;
2. target logical gate set and connectivity/routing model;
3. precision/error allocation and rotation-synthesis procedure;
4. ancilla and scheduling rules, including whether parity ladders may be shared/cancelled;
5. baselines: donor/original TARE where faithfully runnable, unrestricted R6M, support<=2 R6M, support<=1 RED control, and at least one current Pauli compiler such as Symphony/PHOENIX when the semantic objective is comparable;
6. metrics: exact R6M objective, candidate count, compile wall time/RSS, logical 2q gates/depth, arbitrary-angle rotations, synthesized T count/T depth if the precision model is frozen, ancillas, and normalization/subnormalization cost;
7. null controls where support<=2 changes no compiled resource, and a case where a current baseline remains better.

Allowed interpretation should stay fail-closed: `Q1_RESOURCE_VALUE_MATERIAL`, `Q1_NORMAL_FORM_VALUE_ONLY`, `Q1_RESOURCE_VALUE_NULL`, or `CANNOT_CHECK_FAITHFUL_RESOURCE_MODEL`. Until this packet is executed, #1449 supports a **conditional logical-count identity and normal-form significance only**.
